      "knowledge_point": "Solving Trigonometric Equations Involving Cosecant Under a Modified Domain",
      "problem": "Given that ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ are the solutions to the equation $\\operatorname{csc}⁡x=\\frac{5}{4}$ for $-{180}^{∘}\\le x<{180}^{∘},$ what is the numerical value of ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2},$ rounded to the nearest integer?",
      "worked_solution": "Recall that $\\operatorname{csc}⁡x=\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x},$ therefore the given equation is equivalent to\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡x=\\frac{4}{5}.\n$$\n\nNow, we have to find the principal value:\n\n$$\nx=\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(\\frac{4}{5})=(53.130\\,1…)^{∘}≈{53.130}^{∘}\n$$\n\nSince ${53.130}^{∘}$ lies inside the given domain, our first solution is ${x}_{1}={53.130}^{∘}.$\n\nOur first solution lies in the first quadrant and has a reference angle of ${\\theta }_{R}={53.130}^{∘}.$ Since $\\operatorname{sin}⁡x>0,$ the second solution must lie in the second quadrant, and it also has a reference angle ${\\theta }_{R}={53.130}^{∘}.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978818/assets/605af77803fb027c09833b50801fe4b8e6a42a2b623af94a732d0f2f222f9f4a.png)\n\nSince the second solution ${x}_{2}$ lies in the $2$nd quadrant, we can find it using the reference angle as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2} & ={180}^{∘}-{\\theta }_{R} \\\\  & ={180}^{∘}-{53.130}^{∘} \\\\  & ={126.870}^{∘}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solutions are $x={53.130}^{∘},{126.870}^{∘}.$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}≈53.130\\cdot 126.870≈6\\,741.\n$$\n\nrounded to the nearest integer.",
