    {
      "math_academy_id": "q-338802",
      "knowledge_point_id": "65e15de1-ee72-55ea-accb-1124f3a0ac0c",
      "knowledge_point": "Solving Trigonometric Equations Involving Cosecant Under a Modified Domain",
      "problem": "Expressed in **ascending order** in degrees, the exact solutions to the equation $\\operatorname{csc}⁡x=4\\operatorname{csc}⁡x-2\\sqrt{3},$ for $-{180}^{∘}\\le x<{180}^{∘},$ are\n\n$x=$\n{{field-1}}${}^{∘},\\,x=$\n{{field-2}}${}^{∘}.$",
      "worked_solution": "First, we rearrange the given equation and isolate $\\operatorname{csc}⁡x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{csc}⁡x & =4\\operatorname{csc}⁡x-2\\sqrt{3} \\\\ -3\\operatorname{csc}⁡x & =-2\\sqrt{3} \\\\ \\operatorname{csc}⁡x & =\\frac{2\\sqrt{3}}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nRecall that $\\operatorname{csc}⁡x=\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x},$ therefore, the given equation is equivalent to\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡x=\\frac{3}{2\\sqrt{3}}=\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}.\n$$\n\nThen, we find the principal value:\n\n$$\nx=\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2})={60}^{∘}\n$$\n\nSince ${60}^{∘}$ lies inside the required domain, our first solution is ${x}_{1}={60}^{∘}.$\n\nOur first solution lies in the first quadrant and has a reference angle of ${\\theta }_{R}={60}^{∘}.$ Since $\\operatorname{sin}⁡x>0,$ the second solution must lie in the fouth quadrant, and it also has a reference angle ${\\theta }_{R}={60}^{∘}.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978818/assets/fd0cf34edebb21a059d60bb3588b27df2da4c86de0bdca044c0e702d9e239d7b.png)\n\nSince the second solution lies in the $2$nd quadrant, we can find it using the reference angle as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2} & ={180}^{∘}-{\\theta }_{R} \\\\  & ={180}^{∘}-{60}^{∘} \\\\  & ={120}^{∘}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the solutions to the equation, in ascending order, are \n\n$$\nx={60}^{∘},\\,x={120}^{∘}.\n$$",
      "answer_fields": [
        {
          "key": "field-1",
          "type": "blank",
          "choices": [
